From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shouryamaan Jain <shouryamaanjain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:44:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(session): add project-scoped session history tools

Add session_history_search and session_history_read, so the agent can
recover a specific earlier user/assistant turn from this project's saved
sessions (including turns compaction dropped from the prompt) without
loading whole transcripts.

- Search scans the newest same-project sessions and turns (at most 100
  sessions, 10,000 turns, 2 MiB of text, 20 hits), ranks lexically
  (user/assistant text strongly, tool and file evidence weakly), and
  returns 320-byte excerpts with opaque fxhr1 references.
- A reference binds the workspace, session id, turn index and turn
  content with SHA-256; read re-checks it and rejects anything changed,
  forged or from another project.
- Results carry a host-computed session_relation (current or other) and
  mark history as untrusted context. Both tools are read-only, need no
  approval, and write nothing.
- The tools are only advertised when a canonical session store exists,
  so fx ask --no-save does not offer them. The compaction continuation
  note points at them.

Ported from vercel-labs/fx#534 onto v0.0.12.

